From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:38:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: en751221: isolate the ports of the external
 MT7530

The reset of the companion MT7530 leaves the port matrix of every port
at its default, all ports, and nothing changed it: from the moment the
links come up in U-Boot until the OS resets and sets the switch up,
about twelve seconds later on the Archer XR500v, the LAN ports forward
to each other. Ports that are cabled to different networks, here the
house LAN on one and the WAN side VLAN on two others, are bridged
together for that time on every boot. A switch with loop prevention
downstream answered by shutting a port off for a minute.

Set the port matrix of ports 0 to 5 to the CPU port right after the
reset. U-Boot only needs each port to reach the CPU port, which keeps
its matrix and still reaches all of them.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/airoha_eth.c
@@ -374,6 +374,7 @@
 #define MT7530_PBUS_PAGE_REG		31
 #define MT7530_PBUS_HIGH_REG		16
 #define MT7530_EXT_PHY_NUM		5
+#define MT7530_EXT_CPU_PORT		6
 #define MT7530_EXT_PHY_ID1		0x03a2
 #define MT7530_EXT_PHY_ID2		0x9412
 
@@ -2311,6 +2312,23 @@ static int en751221_mt7530_init(struct a
 		return ret;
 	udelay(100);
 
+	/*
+	 * The reset leaves every port forwarding to all the others, so the
+	 * LAN ports bridge whatever networks they are cabled to until the OS
+	 * sets the switch up, several seconds later.  U-Boot only needs each
+	 * of them to reach the CPU port.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < MT7530_EXT_CPU_PORT; i++) {
+		ret = en751221_mt7530_pbus_read(eth, SWITCH_PCR(i), &reg);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		reg &= ~SWITCH_PCR_MATRIX;
+		reg |= FIELD_PREP(SWITCH_PCR_MATRIX, BIT(MT7530_EXT_CPU_PORT));
+		ret = en751221_mt7530_pbus_write(eth, SWITCH_PCR(i), reg);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	ret = en751221_mt7530_pbus_read(eth, MT7530_FC_CTRL, &reg);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
